  "verdict": "RT (conformal-log) entanglement is a CRITICAL-LINE phenomenon. The conformal form S(L)=(c_eff/3)log[(N/pi)sin(pi L/N)] best-fits at p~0.16 (c_eff~4.45>0) -- the RT/CFT signature, the same functional form AdS_3/CFT_2 RT gives and the HaPPY code realises as a hyperbolic min-cut (Ch.5). It is FLANKED by a VOLUME-law (linear) phase at small p [0.05, 0.1] and a trivial AREA-law (const) phase at large p [0.3]. So the monitored substrate carries RT structure ONLY on the critical line, NOT in the area-law phase -- where the one-knob lock (p=1/2) sits. TWO payoffs: (1) CONFIRMS, from the path-integral / monitored perspective, the book's independent Ch.5 finding that the RT relation holds only in an intermediate 'code-state regime' (eta_c~0.5 there, breaking when under- or over-scrambled) and that Einstein dynamics is a FINE-TUNING condition, not generic -- a critical point is measure-zero, exactly 'not generic'. (2) OPENS the reading 'gravitation as a phase transition': gravity (RT) is the critical line between the classical (area/frozen, where the lock lives) and scrambled (volume) phases of the scramble-vs-self-monitor competition. HONEST SCOPE: this matches the conformal SCALING (the level at which RT computes entropy); it does not by itself prove full wedge reconstruction / perfect-tensor structure. The MIPT conformal critical point is established physics (li2018; skinner2019; zabalo2020); the CWF content is the identification with the gravity/RT regime and the fine-tuning confirmation.",
  "honesty": "Matches the conformal RT SCALING S~(c/3)log (the level RT computes), not full wedge reconstruction. MIPT conformal critical point is established (li2018/skinner2019/zabalo2020); CWF content = identification with the gravity/RT regime + confirmation that RT is a fine-tuned (critical, measure-zero) condition, matching Ch.5's A3b 'intermediate code-state regime' and the 'Einstein = fine-tuning, not generic' verdict."
